        {
            "id": "13",
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "\n",
                "If your eQTL mapping DataFrame has the relevant columns in a different place, you need to use the optional arguments `colX` (for the gene expression IDs) and `colG` (for the eQTL genotype IDs) to specify either the relevant columns index or name:\n",
                ""
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "14",
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "dP = findr(dm, dgm, dpm; colX=2, colG=1, FDR=0.1, method=\"kde\");"
            ],
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "execution_count": 1
        },
        {
            "id": "15",
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "\n",
                "or"
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "16",
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "dP = findr(dm, dgm, dpm; colX=\"GENE_ID\", colG=\"SNP_ID\", FDR=0.1, method=\"kde\");"
            ],
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "execution_count": 1
        },
        {
            "id": "17",
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "\n",
                "Any other columns in the eQTL mapping DataFrame (such as association summary statistics) are ignored.\n",
                "\n",
                "### Bipartite causal inference\n",
                "\n",
                "In some applications, we have multiple omics datasets from the same samples, and may be interested in causal inference from one set of variables to another one. In the GEUVADIS study for instance, we may be interested in inferring causal interactions between microRNAs and target genes. To infer interactions *from* microRNAs *to* mRNAs, run:\n",
                ""
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "18",
            "cell_type": "code",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "dP = findr(dt, dm, dgm, dpm; FDR=0.1)"
            ],
